b40301d and Counter c4275588. Ruling 163de663 requires this raise after a signing. The signed 0.5.0 identifiers live in the packets and the trust rows, and this head changes neither.\n\n## What I read besides\n\nThe LC-1 note gains an LC-5 section. It lists:\n\n- both packets, with their byte counts, blobs, SHA-256 values, releases and presentations;\n- the five trust rows and the 0.6.0 opening;\n- the red;\n- how a 0.5.0 install meets the screen rows.\n\nAn install opens a new item and a new application scope (`application-install.ts:47`, `:122`, `:240`). The older item stays active, so each screen keeps serving it until a later head moves its row. So the deployment and the install take no screen down.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- The red, in `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-17-lc5-red/`. With the packets and main's trust rows, the reproduction test fails \"dap-lending must trust each committed packet exactly once\" (3 rows, 5 packets).\n- The gate, END 004e3d51. `gate.txt` names head 4b78c2bb and tree 783ff220 with 0 changed files. Plain 4998 passed with 1 skipped, and Native 1165 passed with 2 skipped. Lost crossings were 0, and the log ends \"gate passed\".\n- Scope. The 13 artifacts name the head, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 830d134a 4b78c2bb`.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 2 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n- Wake rate. The head adds no alarm, scheduled pass or retry. A deployment turns the archive on for any new installed 0.5.0 scope at the existing AR-1 rate.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The change follows the pattern that LC-2 and LC-4 set: committed signed bytes, one trust row each, and the reproduction test that ties them together.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\n## For the planner\n\nAfter the deployment, a 0.5.0 install in counter-witness opens a new item with fresh application state. `counter.inguz.space` keeps serving the 0.4.0 item until the SH head moves its screen row to the new item and presentation 9334159c. NF-7 needs that row, because the 0.4.0 bundle still holds the old gateway rule.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing, install or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fff85e93b9b2f6de070ca0c772842f9eb5318602","binding":"assigned","head":"4b78c2bbd0656f1f409b45476503a176407bb460","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:120cfac95a6a06e2cd488163b26a7072a2826216\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2c24be6c5c950dc876e9c96de6a2cd8eddb901bf\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d9dcb9ab769463d858c74017dae9a23f7f9e45c2","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}